From 979d62f7bc5384489719cccd50668716d7bceb57 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mark-vis <118430440+mark-vis@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:48:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/14] Give captions that do not step their counter a unique
 target

A caption that does not step its counter (\@captionstepfalse in
caption/before, e.g., for a continued float) and has no float target
now gets a target with a unique name: \theH<counter> with the suffix
*<n>, counted per name (figure.1*1, figure.1*2, ...), never a second
figure.1. Before this commit such a caption made no target at all.

\@kernel@caption@unique{<counter>}{<code>} executes <code> while
\theH<counter> gives the next unique name, so code that makes the
target of such a caption itself (with \@captiontargetfalse) gets the
same names as the kernel, without gaps. It is defined in the release
block of \@kernel@caption ("caption interface copies"), so a roll-back
undefines it.

New test caption-interface-003 (the kernel's unique targets, also for a
counter without \theH<counter>, and \@kernel@caption@unique) and
latex-lab float-024 (the real hyperref plugs without \DocumentMetadata:
continued captions in and outside of floats, no duplicate
destinations). caption-interface-001 shows the new target of its
continued caption; caption-interface-002 checks that
\@kernel@caption@unique is undefined after a roll-back.
